-- vpme.de QuadDrum + Expander
-- Four-voice analog drum module, CV-controlled (no MIDI).
--   4 trigger inputs   → trig each voice (we drive these from FHX-8GT)
--   8 CV inputs        → assignable destinations (set on the module itself)
--
-- After `load qd`, the following pattern lanes become available:
--   qd1..qd4    fire the four voice triggers
--   qdc1..qdc8  modulate the eight assignable CV inputs
--
-- Default routing (adjust to your patch):
--   QD voices 1-4 → FHX-8GT outputs 5-8  (assumes Rample claims 1-4)
--                  on MIDI channels 14-17 (after Rample drum kit on 10-13)
--   QD CV inputs 1-8 → cv-router buses 0-7 (typically ADAT → ESX-8CV;
--                      change to other buses if your patch differs)

-- Trigger MCVs on the FH-2: gate-only, one per voice.
fh2-gate 4 69 14
fh2-gate 5 70 15
fh2-gate 6 71 16
fh2-gate 7 72 17

midi-device fh2 "FH-2"

-- Trigger pattern lanes: short notes on dedicated channels.
bind qd1 midi-note fh2 14 60 100 50
bind qd2 midi-note fh2 15 60 100 50
bind qd3 midi-note fh2 16 60 100 50
bind qd4 midi-note fh2 17 60 100 50

-- CV pattern lanes: each emits a numeric pattern on its bus.
-- The destination on the QD module is whatever you've assigned the
-- corresponding CV input to (pitch, decay, FM, snap, etc.).
bind qdc1 cv 0
bind qdc2 cv 1
bind qdc3 cv 2
bind qdc4 cv 3
bind qdc5 cv 4
bind qdc6 cv 5
bind qdc7 cv 6
bind qdc8 cv 7
